Subject: WPE: Phoenix build configuration: OpenSSL digests, static libWPEWebKit, multi-call program hook

WPE hard-requires libgcrypt and libtasn1 even with ENABLE_WEB_CRYPTO=OFF (PAL's SHA digests
and WebCore's key classes, referenced by SerializedScriptValue, are their users then). On Phoenix
use OpenSSL, already linked for glib-networking: USE_OPENSSL instead of USE_GCRYPT, PAL's
CryptoDigestOpenSSL.cpp and WebCore's OpenSSL crypto sources (platform/OpenSSL.cmake).
libWPEWebKit is STATIC (no shared libraries on Phoenix; CMake would turn SHARED into STATIC on its
own, but WebKit's sub-target objects only reach a shared link). A static libWebKit does not carry
the frameworks it is made of, so its executables link them (WebProcess/NetworkProcess_FRAMEWORKS)
and it must not depend on the auxiliary executables (a cycle). PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR adds the
out-of-tree multi-call program (the phoenix-rtos-ports webkit_wpe port's files/launcher);
WPE_PHOENIX_DEFAULT_EXECUTABLE is its install path.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 981edf67..2c1ca510 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -74,6 +74,12 @@ endif ()
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 add_subdirectory(Source)
 
+# Phoenix-RTOS: the static multi-call browser program (UI + WebProcess + NetworkProcess in
+# one ELF), kept outside this tree (the phoenix-rtos-ports webkit_wpe port's files/launcher).
+if (PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR)
+    add_subdirectory(${PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR} ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/PhoenixBrowser)
+endif ()
+
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Add tools
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
